**PR E — `ta-gate-observability`** (P0; I-5 half 2). Off `main` (`bf8fd8d9`), independent of C/D.
Plan: `planning/ta-gate-observability-plan.md`. Summary:
- **Problem:** analyzer registration is frozen at controller startup (`cmd/main.go:533`
  `throughputAnalyzerEnabled` → `RegisterAnalyzer`, frozen after `StartOptimizeLoop` at
  `cmd/main.go:544`). If an operator edits the saturation configmap at runtime to enable TA, the
  change is silently ignored until the controller restarts. A′ landed half 1 (startup log when
  the gate is false); half 2 (runtime edit ignored) is unaddressed.
- **Decision (Dean, this session):** ship the **stopgap** for 0.9 — controller restart is
  acceptable for 0.9. When the live configmap reconciler detects the live TA-enabled state
  differs from the frozen registration decision, emit a **K8s Warning event + log line that
  explicitly tells the operator to restart the controller**. Wiring exists:
  `internal/controller/configmap_reconciler.go` already holds a `Recorder record.EventRecorder`
  (precedent: `K8SEventUnattributedReadyPods`); need to capture the startup registration decision
  and compare it on each reconcile.
- **Dev guide (Type 4, required):** document the new warning behavior in
  `docs/developer-guide/throughput-analyzer.md`.
- **NO WVA user-guide change.** Operator-facing "TA is opt-in + restart-required" content goes to
  the **llm-d/llm-d repo** (WVA config docs/values) — see cross-repo item below.
- **"Disabled by default" needs no code** — verified true this session at all three layers:
  (a) startup gate `throughputAnalyzerEnabled` returns false when TA absent from config;
  (b) shipped `config/base/manager/saturation-scaling-configmap.yaml` default analyzers block
  lists only `- name: saturation, score: 1.0` (no throughput entry); (c) per-cycle
  `effectiveEnabled` fall-through returns false (A′). A′ already has
  `TestThroughputAnalyzerEnabled` covering the default-off gate.
- Superseded later by `wva-analyzer-lifecycle` (which removes the frozen-registration gate
  entirely and absorbs I-5 half 2 properly); PR E is the 0.9 stopgap only.

